%N A399336 The binomial matrix of the Jacobsthal numbers, square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A399336 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A399336 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A399336 A(n, n) = J(n) := A001045(n), the Jacobsthal numbers.
%F A399336 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * J(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
